<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24698" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαδέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bind on either side,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὸ πλοῖον ἀμφοτέρωθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.29
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.154
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὰ χαλκεῖα ταινίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Aud.</u>
					802a40
				</span></i>
			; <i>bandage,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.18.2
			</span></i>; <i>put in chains,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1423.9
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴ διαδεδεμένη ἐν τῷ σώματι</span>”
				<i>fast-bound,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					82e
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἱμάτια ταῖς λαιαῖς</span>
			<i>bind, wrap them</i> round <i>their</i> left arms, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				86
			</span></i>: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαδεῖσθαι καυσίαις</span>
			<i>bind one's head</i> (with a diadem), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				41
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ διαδούμενος</span>
			<i>the boy binding his hair,</i> a famous statue by Polyclitus,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				34.55
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαδησάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.489f
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαδεδέσθαι τὴν κεφαλὴν
				διαδήματι, μίτρᾳ,</span>
			<i>have one's</i> head <i>bound</i> with . ., <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				12.3
			</span></i>.</div>
